From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: harden RX DMA/scatter-gather, zero-copy fast paths, WPA/WEP/RRM/QoS sanity, and ioctl bounds

Backport and harden critical data-path, offload, crypto, and ioctl bounds
defects in mt_wifi 7.6.6.1 for Linux 6.6 on filogic_mtwifi (MT7981/MT7986):
- Fix hif_pci BUF_ZERO heap overflow (build_skb_len - SKB_BUF_HEADROOM_RSV),
  bound RX scatter-gather DMA copies against RxBufferSize and max_buf_len, add
  dma_sync_single_for_cpu in non-WED scatter copy, shrink headroom zeroing to
  min(SKB_BUF_HEADROOM_RSV, 64), and guard token_rx_dmad_init return bounds.
- Harden token_rx_deinit/init/lookup/update against token exhaustion or OOB IDs.
- Enable SKB zero-copy fast paths: needed_headroom >= 64 on new netdevs,
  a4_clone_packet skb_clone, and unshared RtmpVlanPktCopy writable fast-path.
- Reject BMC/unmapped WCID packets in warp_proxy client_hw_tx_allow, use bounded
  scnprintf in dump_raw, check warp_ring_init return, and fix ap_data func_idx.
- Fix dead WDS/APCLI lookup checks in rt_profile, WEP key/length underflow,
  RSNXE bounds, 512B EAPOL KeyData capacity + AES_Key_Unwrap bounds/return check,
  CSPRNG get_random_bytes in GenRandom, SiteSurvey SecurityStr stack overflow
  and row rollback, MacTableStaInfo need_send reset, RRM/QoS integer underflows,
  and ioctl input/buffer validation in ap_cfg/ap_ioctl/ap_qload/scan/ba_action.

Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
